<title>UK: UK's Blagden buys Cellobond business.</title>
<headline>UK's Blagden buys Cellobond business.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blagden Industries Plc said on Monday it was buying the the Cellobond Phenolics business of B.P. Chemicals Ltd for 13 million stg in cash.  </p>
<p>Blagden will finance the acquisition from existing cash and debt resources and called the purchase a &quot;significant step&quot; in developing its Blagden's manufactured chemicals business.</p>
<p>Cellobond produces a range of phenolformaldehyde resins and had a turnover of 15.9 million stg in 1996. B.P. Chemicals is a division of British Petroleum Plc.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
